{"audio": "john-21.opus", "voice": "Davis", "duration_ms": 235733, "sentences": [{"start_ms": 0, "end_ms": 2933, "text": "John, Chapter Twenty-One."}, {"start_ms": 2933, "end_ms": 10000, "text": "After these things Jesus shewed himself again to the disciples at the sea of Tiberias; and on this wise shewed he himself."}, {"start_ms": 10000, "end_ms": 19200, "text": "There were together Simon Peter, and Thomas called Didymus, and Nathanael of Cana in Galilee, and the sons of Zebedee, and two other of his disciples."}, {"start_ms": 19200, "end_ms": 22533, "text": "Simon Peter saith unto them, I go a fishing."}, {"start_ms": 22533, "end_ms": 25733, "text": "They say unto him, We also go with thee."}, {"start_ms": 25733, "end_ms": 30800, "text": "They went forth, and entered into a ship immediately; and that night they caught nothing."}, {"start_ms": 30800, "end_ms": 37733, "text": "But when the morning was now come, Jesus stood on the shore: but the disciples knew not that it was Jesus."}, {"start_ms": 37733, "end_ms": 41600, "text": "Then Jesus saith unto them, Children, have ye any meat?"}, {"start_ms": 41600, "end_ms": 43467, "text": "They answered him, No."}, {"start_ms": 43467, "end_ms": 48000, "text": "And he said unto them, Cast the net on the right side of the ship, and ye shall find."}, {"start_ms": 48000, "end_ms": 52800, "text": "They cast therefore, and now they were not able to draw it for the multitude of fishes."}, {"start_ms": 52800, "end_ms": 57733, "text": "Therefore that disciple whom Jesus loved saith unto Peter, It is the Lord."}, {"start_ms": 57733, "end_ms": 65733, "text": "Now when Simon Peter heard that it was the Lord, he girt his fisher's coat unto him, (for he was naked,) and did cast himself into the sea."}, {"start_ms": 65733, "end_ms": 74667, "text": "And the other disciples came in a little ship; (for they were not far from land, but as it were two hundred cubits,) dragging the net with fishes."}, {"start_ms": 74667, "end_ms": 81200, "text": "As soon then as they were come to land, they saw a fire of coals there, and fish laid thereon, and bread."}, {"start_ms": 81200, "end_ms": 86000, "text": "Jesus saith unto them, Bring of the fish which ye have now caught."}, {"start_ms": 86000, "end_ms": 95733, "text": "Simon Peter went up, and drew the net to land full of great fishes, an hundred and fifty and three: and for all there were so many, yet was not the net broken."}, {"start_ms": 95733, "end_ms": 98267, "text": "Jesus saith unto them, Come and dine."}, {"start_ms": 98267, "end_ms": 102400, "text": "And none of the disciples durst ask him, Who art thou?"}, {"start_ms": 102400, "end_ms": 104000, "text": "knowing that it was the Lord."}, {"start_ms": 104000, "end_ms": 109467, "text": "Jesus then cometh, and taketh bread, and giveth them, and fish likewise."}, {"start_ms": 109467, "end_ms": 115200, "text": "This is now the third time that Jesus shewed himself to his disciples, after that he was risen from the dead."}, {"start_ms": 115200, "end_ms": 121467, "text": "So when they had dined, Jesus saith to Simon Peter, Simon, son of Jonas, lovest thou me more than these?"}, {"start_ms": 121467, "end_ms": 126133, "text": "He saith unto him, Yea, Lord; thou knowest that I love thee."}, {"start_ms": 126133, "end_ms": 128533, "text": "He saith unto him, Feed my lambs."}, {"start_ms": 128533, "end_ms": 134000, "text": "He saith to him again the second time, Simon, son of Jonas, lovest thou me?"}, {"start_ms": 134000, "end_ms": 138133, "text": "He saith unto him, Yea, Lord; thou knowest that I love thee."}, {"start_ms": 138133, "end_ms": 140667, "text": "He saith unto him, Feed my sheep."}, {"start_ms": 140667, "end_ms": 145200, "text": "He saith unto him the third time, Simon, son of Jonas, lovest thou me?"}, {"start_ms": 145200, "end_ms": 149733, "text": "Peter was grieved because he said unto him the third time, Lovest thou me?"}, {"start_ms": 149733, "end_ms": 154267, "text": "And he said unto him, Lord, thou knowest all things; thou knowest that I love thee."}, {"start_ms": 154267, "end_ms": 157200, "text": "Jesus saith unto him, Feed my sheep."}, {"start_ms": 157200, "end_ms": 172800, "text": "Verily, verily, I say unto thee, When thou wast young, thou girdedst thyself, and walkedst whither thou wouldest: but when thou shalt be old, thou shalt stretch forth thy hands, and another shall gird thee, and carry thee whither thou wouldest not."}, {"start_ms": 172800, "end_ms": 177333, "text": "This spake he, signifying by what death he should glorify God."}, {"start_ms": 177333, "end_ms": 181333, "text": "And when he had spoken this, he saith unto him, Follow me."}, {"start_ms": 181333, "end_ms": 192267, "text": "Then Peter, turning about, seeth the disciple whom Jesus loved following; which also leaned on his breast at supper, and said, Lord, which is he that betrayeth thee?"}, {"start_ms": 192267, "end_ms": 197467, "text": "Peter seeing him saith to Jesus, Lord, and what shall this man do?"}, {"start_ms": 197467, "end_ms": 203067, "text": "Jesus saith unto him, If I will that he tarry till I come, what is that to thee?"}, {"start_ms": 203067, "end_ms": 204533, "text": "follow thou me."}, {"start_ms": 204533, "end_ms": 218400, "text": "Then went this saying abroad among the brethren, that that disciple should not die: yet Jesus said not unto him, He shall not die; but, If I will that he tarry till I come, what is that to thee?"}, {"start_ms": 218400, "end_ms": 226000, "text": "This is the disciple which testifieth of these things, and wrote these things: and we know that his testimony is true."}, {"start_ms": 226000, "end_ms": 235067, "text": "And there are also many other things which Jesus did, the which, if they should be written every one, I suppose that even the world itself could not contain the books that should be written."}, {"start_ms": 235067, "end_ms": 235733, "text": "Amen."}], "words": [{"t": "John,", "s": 1266, "e": 1567, "si": 0}, {"t": "Chapter", "s": 17